---
title: Token refresh
---
sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Token refresh
    accDescr: The browser retries a rejected API call once by exchanging its refresh token at the auth service, then replays the original request. A second rejection logs the user out.

    participant B as Browser
    participant A as API
    participant Auth as Auth service

    B->>A: GET /invoices (expired access token)
    A-->>B: 401 token_expired

    B->>Auth: POST /token (refresh token)
    alt refresh token still valid
        Auth-->>B: 200 new access token
        B->>A: GET /invoices (retry)
        A-->>B: 200 invoices
    else refresh token revoked
        Auth-->>B: 401 invalid_grant
        Note over B: Clear session, redirect to login
    end
